tui-lipan's changes to libghostty-vt 1.0.1, applied by tui-lipan-ghostty-vt-src (and by
tui-lipan-ghostty-vt-sys to a GHOSTTY_VT_SOURCE_DIR tree). Each is marked "tui-lipan patch" in
the source.

1. Alternate-screen shrink keeps the rows at the cursor (PageList.zig, Screen.zig). Upstream
   1.0.1 crops from the top, so a full-screen program loses its top rows on resize.
2. The legacy (mode 2027 off) zero-width append path marks the row dirty, as the clustering path
   does, so a combining mark that arrives in a later write reaches the render state; and it
   keeps VS15/VS16 after any emoji_vs_base, so keycaps (1 FE0F 20E3) keep their selector
   (Terminal.zig).
3. ghostty_terminal_tl_cursor_set and ghostty_terminal_tl_erase_below: cursor placement and
   ED 0 without the VT parser, so a host can edit the grid while the child has left an escape
   sequence unfinished (c/terminal.zig, c/main.zig, lib_vt.zig, terminal.h).

